# Zenith (CloudResourceOptimizationPlatform) — Cursor Rules

## Startup (Tier A only)

**Every thread / session — read only:**
- `ai-docs/STATUS.md`
- `ai-docs/SCRATCHPAD.md`

**Read `ai-docs/AI_MASTER.md` once per thread** — apply PRE → EXECUTE → POST from memory on later messages. Do not re-open it every turn.

**Never read at startup:** `AUDIT_LOG.md`, `AUDIT_LOG_ARCHIVE_*.md`, `PROGRESS_HISTORY.md`, full `docs/`.

---

## PRE-PHASE (before product code)

**Full** (features, multi-file, API, security, ML): update `STATUS.md` + `PROGRESS.md` + `SCRATCHPAD.md`, output `📋 PRE-PHASE COMPLETE`.

**Lightweight** (one-file typo/format/tiny fix): Tier A only, one chat line `Lightweight: …`, skip claim rewrite if task unchanged — see `AI_MASTER.md`.

---

## POST-PHASE (before stop)

**Full:** tests/lint → `STATUS` + `PROGRESS` + `SCRATCHPAD` → append `PROGRESS_HISTORY` (long narrative) → append `AUDIT_LOG` (≤5 bullets). Chat reply ≤5 bullets.

**Lightweight:** lint/test if needed only; skip `AUDIT_LOG` and `PROGRESS_HISTORY` unless user asked.

**Git:** commit/push **only when user asks** or at phase/milestone — not every session.

---

## Anti-waste

- No long session stories in chat or `PROGRESS.md` — use `PROGRESS_HISTORY.md`
- No re-reading `AI_MASTER` or `AUDIT_LOG` each message
- Load `AI_RULES`, `AI_CONTEXT_*`, `DECISIONS` on demand only

---

## Non-negotiables

- Never commit `backend/.env`
- Zero-cost / free-tier — `ai-docs/AI_RULES.md`
- Brand **Zenith** / **ZenithApp**
- Max 2 heavy processes (pytest, npm install, uvicorn, celery)
- Full PRE-PHASE required for security, auth, BYOC, phase work
